<%# Promote a queued item to a priority session, now.
    Posts to WorkBacklogPromotionsController — the browser surface, not the
    API-key surface every agent session holds. Read the honest limits of that
    boundary on the controller: Zimmer's web UI authenticates nobody, so this
    means "came in through a browser", not "a person did it".

    `turbo_confirm` because the click spawns a session and takes a slot; there is
    no undo, only an archive. %>
<%= button_to promote_work_backlog_item_path(row.item, query_params),
    method: :post,
    class: "text-xs px-2 py-1 border border-indigo-300 text-indigo-700 rounded hover:bg-indigo-50 whitespace-nowrap disabled:opacity-50",
    form: { data: { turbo_confirm: "Start #{row.key} now as a priority session? This spawns a zimmer-router session immediately and takes a slot ahead of the spot queue." } } do %>
  Promote
<% end %>
